  "evidence": [
    "Pinned50BA00..50BA27 is39byte helper; native mapped-span inspection finds263 directcalls across21 source TUs. No positive original inline witness found; historical comments alone do not establish mixed policy. Source bitmask_call is forwarding only; has_fac_built_call duplicates the unguarded two-argument facilities-byte predicate with int rather than bool return. One-argument guarded overload must remain distinct."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover genuine bitmask ownership and original call boundaries; retire bitmask_call and consolidate the redundant two-argument facility predicate where source/ABI evidence supports it. Preserve signed truncating division, input-by-value/output-alias semantics, offset-before-mask stores, original quirks, identities and historical claims. Verify all affected callers and full build collateral; no new noinline adapters.",
